---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../site.config';
import { fitTitle, fitDesc } from '../lib/seo';

const title = fitTitle(['Contact the FX & Commodity Almanac: Corrections, Questions']);
const description = fitDesc([
  'Email the FX & Commodity Almanac to report a data error, ask how a figure or method works, or raise a privacy or advertising question. We read every message.',
]);
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/contact/" og="home"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Board', href: '/' }, { name: 'Contact', href: '/contact/' }]}>
  <p class="kicker">Contact</p>
  <h1>How can you contact the almanac?</h1>
  <p id="answer" class="lede">Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. It is the fastest way to report a wrong figure, ask how a number was computed, or raise a privacy question. Please include the page address and the figure you are asking about.</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If a figure differs from the ECB or World Bank original, tell us which page, which figure and where you saw the official value. We check against the source and, if we were wrong, correct the page and note the update date. Before writing, it may help to read the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>: many apparent differences come from cross-rate calculation or from monthly averages versus daily prices.</p>
    <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>
    <p>We cannot give personal financial, tax or trading advice, quote live dealing rates or tell you which provider to use. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
    <h2>Privacy requests</h2>
    <p>For questions about data collected by analytics or advertising on this site, see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> or write to the same address.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
